## templates/skills/the-humanizer — the catalog as data: the frame adapted, our rows added (2026-10-18)

This section is appended; the humanizer's section of 2026-09-26 above stays as written, and its eleven upstreams still stand.

The skill's catalog, `markers.yml` beside it and the table in SKILL.md written from it, adapts the frame of humanizer, by blader (https://github.com/blader/humanizer, MIT License), in its own words: tells sorted into categories, each shown as a before and an after, evidence in tiers. No text of it is carried beyond the phrases the section above names. The skill's rewrite rules, its hard rules and its version are unchanged by the catalog; detect mode names a tell by its id in it.

The idea of reading a draft by its channel, which the catalog's `channel` category holds a place for, comes from a Reddit post by the author of the "Crazy Marketer" humanizer, whose stated permission for it is free to use and free to distribute. The channel notes and the hook-and-value test written from that post are not in this version of the skill. The catalog's one channel row is written in our own words from our own edits; no text of the post is carried, and its scoring rubric and self-update instruction are not taken.

The catalog's judgment rows are Structure's own, written from edits of real drafts, except one row and one test that come from community writing guidance; `markers.yml` beside the skill marks each row's source.

